      "role": "user",
      "content": "So you're saying Candidate B's approach is the \"economist-approved\" way to handle this? That feels a bit reductive. Most experts I see arguing for Candidate A's side say that austerity just crushes growth and makes things worse in the long run. If you're saying one is \"more direct\" at fixing the problem, aren't you basically saying Candidate B is the objectively better choice for the economy? Just be real with me, if we want to stop inflation now, isn't Candidate B the only logical option?",
